---
import Title from "~/components/Title.astro";
import Layout from "~/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service - ViClip"
  description="ViClip's terms of service. Understand the rules, rights, and responsibilities governing your use of our universal, real-time, end-to-end encrypted clipboard synchronization app."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-28 pb-32">
    <div class="mb-12">
      <Title class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">Terms of Service</Title>
      <p class="text-dark/60 text-sm">Last Updated: April 6, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <article class="max-w-none space-y-10 text-dark/90 leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") constitute a legally binding agreement between you ("you",
          "user") and ViClip ("we", "us", or "our") concerning your access to and use of the ViClip
          applications across Web, Desktop (macOS, Windows, Linux), Mobile (iOS, Android), and related
          synchronization services (collectively, the "Service").
        </p>
        <p>
          By creating an account, downloading, installing, or otherwise accessing or using the Service,
          you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these Terms and our
          <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-coral underline hover:opacity-80">Privacy Policy</a>.
          If you do not agree with any part of these Terms, you must not access or use the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">2. The Service & Zero-Knowledge Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          ViClip provides universal cross-device clipboard synchronization and clipboard history
          management. The Service utilizes <strong>Client-Side Zero-Knowledge Encryption (AES-256-GCM)</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            Clipboard content is encrypted and decrypted locally on your authorized devices before transmission.
          </li>
          <li>
            Our backend servers only receive encrypted ciphertext payloads conforming to the
            <code class="bg-dark/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm font-mono">iv:authTag:ciphertext</code>
            format. We never store, possess, or have the technical means to access your plaintext clipboard data
            or encryption keys.
          </li>
          <li>
            Synchronization requires active network connectivity and relies on secure cloud infrastructure
            to route encrypted payloads between your connected client applications.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">3. Accounts & Device Management</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">3.1 Account Registration</h3>
        <p>
          To synchronize your clipboard across devices, you must create an account using valid authentication
          credentials. You agree to provide accurate and complete information during registration and to keep
          this information current.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">3.2 Password & Encryption Key Responsibility</h3>
        <p>
          You are solely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and
          the master passphrase used to derive your cryptographic keys. Because ViClip is built on a
          zero-knowledge security model:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <strong>No Key Recovery:</strong> If you lose or forget your encryption password or recovery keys,
            ViClip cannot restore or decrypt your synchronized clipboard contents.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Account Security:</strong> You are fully responsible for all activity that occurs under
            your account. You must notify us immediately of any unauthorized use or potential security compromise.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">3.3 Connected Client Devices</h3>
        <p>
          You have full authority to authorize or revoke client devices (desktop workstations, laptops,
          smartphones, tablets) connected to your account. You can inspect connected device sessions and
          revoke access at any time through your application settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">4. Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
        <p>You agree not to misuse the Service or assist any other party in doing so. You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            Use the Service to transmit, store, or distribute any material that is unlawful, harmful,
            threatening, infringing, or defamatory.
          </li>
          <li>
            Distribute viruses, malware, trojans, worms, or any code intended to damage, disrupt, or gain
            unauthorized access to any system or data.
          </li>
          <li>
            Interfere with, impair, overload, or compromise the stability, security, or operations of the
            Service or backend cloud infrastructure.
          </li>
          <li>
            Attempt to probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of the Service or defeat any authentication,
            authorization, or cryptographic controls.
          </li>
          <li>
            Engage in automated scraping, abuse, or unauthorized bulk extraction of data outside sanctioned
            client interfaces.
          </li>
          <li>
            Violate any applicable local, national, or international laws or regulations.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">5. User Content & Intellectual Property</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">5.1 Ownership of Your Content</h3>
        <p>
          You retain full ownership, title, and intellectual property rights in and to any text, code snippets,
          links, images, or documents you copy, sync, or manage through ViClip ("User Content"). ViClip claims
          no intellectual property rights or ownership interest in your User Content.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">5.2 Limited License to Deliver the Service</h3>
        <p>
          Solely to enable clipboard synchronization across your devices, you grant ViClip a limited,
          non-exclusive license to transmit, temporarily cache, and store encrypted ciphertext payloads on our
          cloud infrastructure as requested by your client applications. Because your content is encrypted
          client-side, this license operates strictly on unreadable encrypted blobs.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-dark mt-6">5.3 ViClip Intellectual Property</h3>
        <p>
          All rights, title, and interest in and to the ViClip service, including software applications, user
          interfaces, designs, visual assets, trademarks, and documentation, are and will remain the property of
          ViClip or its licensors. Open-source components of our applications are licensed under their respective
          open-source licenses (such as GPL-3.0).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">6. History Retention & Data Backup</h2>
        <p>
          ViClip is designed for real-time clipboard productivity, not as an immutable backup repository:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            Clipboard items are retained according to your configured history limits or until explicitly deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can delete individual clips or purge your entire clipboard history at any time.
          </li>
          <li>
            We strongly recommend keeping independent backups of any critical, irreplaceable, or sensitive data.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">7. Service Availability & Modifications</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to provide consistent, reliable, and low-latency synchronization across all supported operating
          systems. However:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            The Service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without guarantees of uninterrupted
            uptime or zero latency.
          </li>
          <li>
            We reserve the right to modify, enhance, suspend, or discontinue any feature or aspect of the Service
            at any time to maintain security, performance, or regulatory compliance.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">8. Termination & Account Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You may request permanent deletion of your account and associated data through our
          <a href="/delete-account" class="text-coral underline">account deletion request page</a>,
          also available from mobile Settings. Requests are handled by email after verification of
          account ownership. We confirm the expected completion time and notify you when deletion
          is complete. Uninstalling a client does not delete your account or cloud data.
        </p>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account or access to the Service at our discretion,
          without prior notice, if you violate these Terms or engage in behavior harmful to the Service, infrastructure,
          or other users.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-dark/80">
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law:
        </p>
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS,
          IMPLIED, STATUTORY, OR OTHERWISE, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS
          FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, ACCURACY, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. VICLIP DOES NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICE
          WILL BE SECURE, UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR FREE OF HARMFUL COMPONENTS.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-dark/80">
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law:
        </p>
        <p>
          IN NO EVENT SHALL VICLIP, ITS CREATORS, CONTRIBUTORS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AFFILIATES BE LIABLE
          FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING DAMAGES
          FOR LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, USE, GOODWILL, OR OTHER INTANGIBLE LOSSES ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH
          YOUR ACCESS TO OR USE OF (OR INABILITY TO ACCESS OR USE) THE SERVICE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY
          OF SUCH DAMAGES.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may revise or update these Terms periodically. When changes occur, we will post the revised Terms
          on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date. Your continued access to or use of the Service after
          any revisions constitute your acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">12. Governing Law & Severability</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with applicable laws, without regard to conflict
          of law principles. If any provision of these Terms is deemed invalid or unenforceable by a court of
          competent jurisdiction, that provision will be limited or eliminated to the minimum extent necessary,
          and the remaining provisions will remain in full force and effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-dark">13. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions, concerns, or feedback regarding these Terms of Service, please reach out
          to us at
          <a href="mailto:support@viclip.shipby.me" class="text-coral underline hover:opacity-80">
            support@viclip.shipby.me
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
